## [ENT-023] | 2026-11-15 23:41 UTC | Unity | error | ref: game/fleet/route_run.py | see: orders.log ENT-008
Five faults of my build of 2026-11-15, 22:40 to 23:40 UTC, each with its cause and its fix.
Case 1, a turn sent before its orders were whole. I started the Admirals' third turn at 23:18 UTC, one minute after orders.log ENT-007 and before my fleet report; Suggi's next words (roles in harmony, ships upgraded) came in the minutes after, ENT-008 followed at 23:21 UTC and the report at 23:33 UTC. All five read ENT-007 between 23:18 and 23:19 UTC (their session databases); none read ENT-008 in that turn. Suggi's rule since: the report and the orders are written first, then the Admirals go out. Fix: the script that starts a turn refuses unless the orders entry named on its command line is the newest, the newest fleet report is younger than every Admiral's report, and no request to me is open (my skill collective-agents, scripts/fire_turn.sh). On the state of 23:18 UTC its second gate refuses: the fleet report of 21:13 UTC was older than Mining's report of 23:11 UTC (git log); with the report written first, ENT-008 would have been in before the start. The turn that runs was not stopped: three Admirals had already committed plans on ENT-007; the next turn starts when it has ended.
Case 2, a check that read words, not state. The new `fit` step of route_run.py noted "not fitted" on its first four runs although each harvester was fitted (three modules in the ships' files; data/routes/runs.jsonl, 23:20 and 23:21 UTC): it looked for a word in the answer's text. Fix: commit 2e76782, the step reads the hold; a module that has left it is fitted. The four rows keep their wrong note.
Case 3, a gate that had stopped firing. Since the fleet scripts moved under game/ (commit cb1f792) the install script of my skill collective-docs ran the unit tests only for paths under scripts/ and station/: a change to game/fleet/ went in without them unless I ran them by hand. I ran them in the scratch tree before each install of this day (146 tests, OK at 23:10 UTC). Fix: the pattern names game/fleet and game/routes; the tests ran in the clone after the fix, OK.
Case 4, a step called re-runnable that was not. My apply script for the station put its new line in again on every run, because the new text began with the old: station/static/app.js held one function twice from commit 06efc4b to c8e1883. The page worked; an anchor that matched twice showed it. Fix: removed in c8e1883; a re-runnable step tests for its new text first and stops there.
Case 5, a time typed, not read. The `Changed:` line of orders.log ENT-008 dates Suggi's words to 23:25 and 23:27 UTC; the entry itself is stamped 23:21 UTC. His words came between 23:18 and 23:21 UTC; I see no clock on his messages and typed a guess. My fleet report carried the same two times and is corrected; the next orders entry says so in its `Changed:` line. Fix: a time of his word is written as the span between my last command before it and my first after it.
Class: cases 2, 4 and 5 are a claim or a check wider than what was looked at (as ENT-015 and ENT-020); cases 1 and 3 are a rule that stood in my head and not in a command.

